#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  READ THIS LINE FIRST: the four commands in docs/release/QUICKSTART.md need
#  NOTHING from this file. `just doctor`, `just setup`, `just up` and `just prove`
#  run on a machine that has never held one of our credentials, which is PL-1, and
#  a proof that quietly depends on an untracked file has not been reproduced by
#  anyone. This file exists so that a stranger can see what each variable WOULD
#  change, not so that they have to fill one in.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `justfile` sets `dotenv-load := false` on purpose, so `just` does NOT read `.env`.
# If you want these in your shell, put them there yourself and say so out loud:
#
#     cp .env.example .env          # .env is gitignored; never commit a filled one
#     set -a ; . ./.env ; set +a    # bash/zsh
#
# Every line below says what BREAKS when it is unset. Where the answer is "nothing",
# it says that too — an example file that implies everything is mandatory teaches a
# reader the opposite of the truth.


# ── 1. The cluster ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Four spellings, one meaning. Every cluster fixture in this repository — all
# twenty-three files that can start a container — checks these FIRST and only reaches
# for Docker when they are all unset. That is the seam trappoint-testkit uses to
# collapse thirteen private clusters into one. Setting any of them points the whole
# suite, `scripts/proof/gate_refusal.py` and `scripts/qa/doctor.py` at that node.
#
# Unset: nothing breaks. The testkit finds or starts the local single node and
# publishes all four itself; the doctor falls back to
# postgresql://root@127.0.0.1:26257/defaultdb?sslmode=disable.
MAINLINE_TEST_DSN=postgresql://root@127.0.0.1:26257/defaultdb?sslmode=disable
TRAPPOINT_DSN=postgresql://root@127.0.0.1:26257/defaultdb?sslmode=disable
COCKROACH_URL=postgresql://root@127.0.0.1:26257/defaultdb?sslmode=disable
CRDB_URL=postgresql://root@127.0.0.1:26257/defaultdb?sslmode=disable

# The same DSN under the name `justfile` uses for it. Unset: nothing breaks; the
# recipes carry the literal.
LOCAL_DSN=postgresql://root@127.0.0.1:26257/defaultdb?sslmode=disable

# Seconds libpq waits per resolved address. Unset: the testkit sets 5 for you. If you
# unset it AND bypass the testkit, a dead node is an infinite wait rather than a
# failure — measured on this machine: 130.1 s to raise unset, 3.1 s at 3. That is the
# difference between a suite that goes red and a suite that wedges.
PGCONNECT_TIMEOUT=5


# ── 2. The image ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Three spellings, one meaning, and the value belongs in compose.yaml, not here.
# Thirty-three modules default to the FLOATING tag `cockroachdb/cockroach:latest-v26.2`
# when these are unset, which is exactly the dev/CI skew the schema fingerprint exists
# to catch. trappoint-testkit exports all three from the `trappoint:crdb-image-pin`
# line in compose.yaml before collection, so in a normal run they are already set.
#
# Unset: nothing breaks — the testkit fills them in. Set BY HAND: you have overridden
# the one version constant, and you own the consequences.
# CRDB_IMAGE=cockroachdb/cockroach:v26.2.5
# MAINLINE_CRDB_IMAGE=cockroachdb/cockroach:v26.2.5
# TRAPPOINT_CRDB_IMAGE=cockroachdb/cockroach:v26.2.5


# ── 3. How the suite obtains a cluster ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# The default for `pytest --crdb=…`: auto | reuse | spawn | none.
#   auto  — reuse a cluster that answers, start exactly one if none does (default)
#   reuse — never start one; what `just test-cluster` and CI want
#   spawn — always this package's own container; what a bisect wants
#   none  — start nothing, and skip every cluster test with a reason in seconds
# Unset: `auto`. Nothing breaks.
# TRAPPOINT_CRDB_MODE=auto

# Set to 1 to destroy the container the testkit started when the session ends.
# Unset: a container the testkit started is LEFT RUNNING, so the next run is instant.
# Nothing breaks either way; the difference is one warm start.
# TRAPPOINT_TESTKIT_TEARDOWN=0


# ── 4. The interpreter that runs the doctor ──────────────────────────────────
#
# `just doctor`, `just pin` and `just up` run `$PYTHON scripts/qa/doctor.py`, and those
# three recipes are the ones that must work BEFORE `just setup` has installed uv.
# Unset: `python`. Set it if your Python 3.13+ is called something else — on many Linux
# distributions that is `python3`.
# PYTHON=python3


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  NOTHING BELOW THIS LINE IS READ BY ANY RECIPE IN docs/release/QUICKSTART.md.
#  These unlock tests that otherwise SKIP with a stated reason. A skip is an honest
#  answer; a fabricated pass is not. Leave them empty and the suite stays green with
#  fewer claims in it, which is the trade this project makes on purpose.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 5. AWS (Bedrock) — optional, never required ──────────────────────────────
#
# Unset: every test marked `requires_aws` skips with its reason. Nothing in the Tier-2
# proof touches AWS, and no recipe in the justfile does either.
# AWS_PROFILE=
# AWS_REGION=ap-southeast-2
# BEDROCK_REGION=ap-southeast-2
# MAINLINE_AWS_LIVE=0
# MAINLINE_AGENT_ALLOW_LIVE=0

# The recall pipeline's provider and its recorded-cassette fallback. Unset: the
# cassette provider is used and no network call is made. Set to a live provider and
# you are paying for tokens on every run.
# MAINLINE_RECALL_PROVIDER=cassette
# MAINLINE_RECALL_ALLOW_NETWORK=0


# ── 6. CockroachDB Cloud — optional, nightly truth check only ────────────────
#
# Unset: `cloud-verify` has nothing to talk to and says so. The local node is the whole
# local proof; Cloud exists to catch what local's MORE PERMISSIVE defaults hide
# (gc.ttlseconds 14400 here against 4500 there — `just gc-align` closes that one).
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy of these. `.env` is gitignored; `.env.example` is not.
# COCKROACH_DSN=
# CC_API_KEY=
# CC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=
# CRDB_CLUSTER=
# CRDB_REGION=
